Go toolchain

Install:
  Install download and JSON tools, select the latest stable official archive, verify SHA256 and register go/gofmt and GOBIN; reuse complete versions.

Upgrade:
  Select and install the current stable version using the same verified archive flow.

Status:
  Report the locally available Go version.

Requirements:
  Ubuntu, APT and a regular user with sudo access. Supported architectures: amd64 and arm64.

Configuration:
  Installation directory: ~/.local/share/go
  Command links and GOBIN: ~/.local/bin
  GOENV must allow persistent Go configuration.
